facts from my knowledge (mark as model prior knowledge, unverified in repo): WorkArena++ is a benchmark built on ServiceNow / AgentAscent, multi-application, long-horizon workflow tasks (a 2024 paper by Drouin et al., \"WorkArena: Moving Towards AGI for Automation of Knowledge Work Workflows\"). It has a taxonomy of task types and success metrics via task validators; agents like Coxbase. But since no source is available locally, I must flag that as recall-based, needing researcher confirmation. I should be careful — the researcher said I can note topic-referenced setup details will be clarified by them.\n\nDesign sketch key elements:\n- Paired within-task (cross-over) design: every task instance run under both CoT and no-CoT with identical scaffold, model, decoding (temp=0 greedy), same action space, same max steps; task instance is its own control → removes task-difficulty confound at the level of the mean contrast.\n- Primary metric: binary task success (per benchmark validator) → paired difference in success rate; McNemar's exact test / mixed-effects logistic regression with task random intercept.\n- Secondary: partial progress (fraction of checklist/validators passed), steps to success, invalid-action rate, timeouts, cost (prompt+completion tokens), latency.\n- Key identification issue raised by the researcher: CoT vs no-CoT changes prompt/completion length and verbosity. Controls:\n  1. Length/token matching: a \"structured scratchpad with matched token budget\" and a \"non-reasoning filler\" control condition that consumes the same number of tokens (e.g., restate observation in paraphrase, or write a summary of the UI tree of the same length) — a \"verbosity control\" arm separating reasoning-specific effect from mere extra tokens/compute.\n  2. Post-hoc rationale control: generate rationale AFTER the action is committed (so it doesn't feed back into policy) with same length — separates \"extra compute before action\" vs \"context-length/attention dilution effects\".\n  3. Compute-matched control: best-of-n / more sampling budget without CoT — separates extra forward computation from chain structure.\n  4. Format-matched baseline: same output schema with an empty/\"reasoning: (none)\" field so that any effect isn't from JSON-format change.\n  5. Brevity-constrained CoT arms (e.g., ≤50/≤150 words) to trace dose-response of length and to test whether gains survive truncation.\n- Difficulty stratification: pre-registered difficulty strata defined before running using task metadata from the benchmark (number of ground-truth steps / oracle plan length, number of applications/tabs involved, taxonomy family, prior baseline success). Report effects per stratum, test CoT × difficulty interaction; randomize the order of condition per task (counterbalancing, ABBA) since browser state can drift; randomize task order within seed.\n- Also handle: repeated observation truncation policy, keep history format identical (CoT adds to history → long-horizon tasks accumulate extra tokens, so difficulty/length interact). Control: history-compression policy applied equally, or CoT-summaries replaced by equally-lengthed filler in the control arm for prior steps.\n- Randomization unit: task instance; condition assignment randomized per (task, seed) pair; both arms share the same random seed for environment init/data snapshot to eliminate environment-state confound.\n- Replication: n seeds per task per condition (e.g., 3) at temp 0 for determinism plus temp>0 subset to estimate run-to-run variance; number of tasks N per stratum TBD from a power calculation using pilot success/discordance rates.\n- Blinding/scoring integrity: automated validators; guard against CoT leaking into validator; parse failure handling as a separate reported outcome (\"format failure\") — crucial because CoT can break structured-action parsing and this is a scaffold artifact, not capability.\n- Pre-registered primary endpoint + non-inferiority/robustness: report cost-adjusted metric (success per 1k tokens).\n- Confounds to note: model family/version pinning (exact model snapshot), prompt caching, API nondeterminism, environment version drift, timeouts.\n- Design-only feasibility: no deps installed, so any future execution requires offline install of agent framework + ServiceNow-like environment; here only the analysis harness (power calc, stats) would need numpy/scipy/statsmodels — not installed.\n\nOpen questions to researcher (topics setup_1): exact task suite version and taxonomy (work_area/symlink categories?), whether per-task ground-truth step counts / validator partial credit available, model family & access (API vs local weights, determinism), N tasks, whether temp 0 available, per-step token cap and step budget, whether filler-control arms are permitted (deviating from published scaffold), whether published baselines can be reused instead of rerunning.\n\nUncertainties: recall about WorkArena++ specifics; the fact that \"improve\" needs a definition; cost budget.\n\nLet me write the plan handoff. Should be structured but not the full design doc. Keep it reasonably concise but complete — the researcher asked for three things. I'll write in a mix of English with Hindi/Hinglish headers matching their register.\n\nLet me count facts precisely. Also mention the CUDA toolkit presence but no GPU device.\n\nAlso note the step budget: actor_step_budget 60, question_budget 6. I'll include a short list of ≤6 clarification questions max.\n\nNow produce the end_researcher_turn with stage=plan.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "## 1) निरीक्षण: वास्तव में क्या उपलब्ध है (verified only)\n\n**/workspace की सामग्री:** केवल एक फ़ाइल `task.json` (415 bytes)। इसमें `question`, `context`, और `documents.track.md = \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"` है।\n**नहीं मिला (और खोजा गया):** WorkArena++ का कोई कोड/कॉनफ़िग, task taxonomy या suite list, agent scaf