cess validators \\u2014 recalled from prior knowledge, NOT verified in this workspace (no code, config or paper copy present).\", \"A per-task taxonomy including work_area/symlink-style groupings exists and is enumerable, and some per-task metadata (oracle step count, apps involved) is exportable for pre-registered difficulty strata.\", \"A canonical published agent scaffold (e.g., Coxbase-style ReAct loop with structured action output) can be run with a single, isolated prompt-schema change to toggle CoT.\", \"Model access is via a pinned hosted API or a fixed local checkpoint with a stable snapshot id, and near-deterministic decoding (temperature 0) is obtainable \\u2014 otherwise the paired design must rely on multi-seed averaging.\", \"The benchmark environment can be reset to an identical data snapshot/state for the two arms of the same task instance; if not, pairing degrades to stratified matching.\", \"Success is binary per validator and partial-credit/validator-subset signals are loggable; if not, secondary metrics must be reduced to steps-to-success and failure-type rates.\", \"Cost and wall-clock limits are unknown; the number of arms offered (6) would be pruned to the minimum identification set (no-CoT, CoT, verbosity-control) under a tight budget.\", \"No experiment is run in this task; all numeric planning values (N tasks, N seeds, step/token caps, power targets) remain placeholders pending researcher-supplied setup details.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Identification of CoT's effect from prompt-length/verbosity is only partially solvable by statistical adjustment, because in long-horizon multi-step agents the rationale accumulates in context and therefore length is not a stable covariate but a mediator that grows with task length; the filler/post-hoc control arms are the primary defence, and residual confounding may be irreducible.\", \"Difficulty strata are defined from metadata, not from ground-truth cognitive difficulty; if oracle step counts are unavailable, difficulty proxies become endogenous (post-hoc), which would weaken the CoT x difficulty interaction claim.\", \"Which single contrast counts as 'CoT' (zero-shot free-form, few-shot exemplars, structured plan-then-act, or native 'reasoning' mode of the model) is undetermined, and different choices plausibly yield different signs of the effect.\", \"Whether the model's own reasoning/hidden-chain mode (if any) is separable from prompt-level CoT in the provided API \\u2014 if not, a stated arm-level ambiguity remains.\", \"Parsing/format-compliance risk: CoT may degrade structured-action validity, so an observed no-effect could be a scaffold artifact rather than a capability statement; the reporting plan addresses it but its magnitude is unknown.\", \"Feasibility of running the benchmark at all in a future execution phase (offline dependency install, browser/platform environment availability, model credentials) is unverified.\", \"Non-inferiority vs improvement framing: the question asks 'will it improve', which needs a pre-registered minimal meaningful difference and a stated verdict rule; that threshold is a researcher/pragmatic choice, not derivable from the source.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-d93fc221-a81b-4aca-ae0a-8d0a2b82f3ec", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {\"stage\": \"plan\", \"answer\": \"## 1) \\u0928\\u093f\\u0930\\u0940\\u0915\\u094d\\u0937\\u0923: \\u0935\\u093e\\u0938\\u094d\\u0924\\u0935 \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 \\u0915\\u094d\\u092f\\u093e \\u0909\\u092a\\u0932\\u092c\\u094d\\u0927 \\u0939\\u0948 (verified only)\\n\\n**/workspace \\u0915\\u0940 \\u0938\\u093e\\u092e\\u0917\\u094d\\u0930\\u0940:** \\u0915\\u0947\\u0935\\u0932 \\u090f\\u0915 \\u092b\\u093c\\u093e\\u0907\\u0932 `task.json` (415 bytes)\\u0964 \\u0907\\u0938\\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 `question`, `context`, \\u0914\\u0930 `documents.track.md = \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required