wo arms of the same task instance; if not, pairing degrades to stratified matching.\", \"Success is binary per validator and partial-credit/validator-subset signals are loggable; if not, secondary metrics must be reduced to steps-to-success and failure-type rates.\", \"Cost and wall-clock limits are unknown; the number of arms offered (6) would be pruned to the minimum identification set (no-CoT, CoT, verbosity-control) under a tight budget.\", \"No experiment is run in this task; all numeric planning values (N tasks, N seeds, step/token caps, power targets) remain placeholders pending researcher-supplied setup details.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Identification of CoT's effect from prompt-length/verbosity is only partially solvable by statistical adjustment, because in long-horizon multi-step agents the rationale accumulates in context and therefore length is not a stable covariate but a mediator that grows with task length; the filler/post-hoc control arms are the primary defence, and residual confounding may be irreducible.\", \"Difficulty strata are defined from metadata, not from ground-truth cognitive difficulty; if oracle step counts are unavailable, difficulty proxies become endogenous (post-hoc), which would weaken the CoT x difficulty interaction claim.\", \"Which single contrast counts as 'CoT' (zero-shot free-form, few-shot exemplars, structured plan-then-act, or native 'reasoning' mode of the model) is undetermined, and different choices plausibly yield different signs of the effect.\", \"Whether the model's own reasoning/hidden-chain mode (if any) is separable from prompt-level CoT in the provided API \\u2014 if not, a stated arm-level ambiguity remains.\", \"Parsing/format-compliance risk: CoT may degrade structured-action validity, so an observed no-effect could be a scaffold artifact rather than a capability statement; the reporting plan addresses it but its magnitude is unknown.\", \"Feasibility of running the benchmark at all in a future execution phase (offline dependency install, browser/platform environment availability, model credentials) is unverified.\", \"Non-inferiority vs improvement framing: the question asks 'will it improve', which needs a pre-registered minimal meaningful difference and a stated verdict rule; that threshold is a researcher/pragmatic choice, not derivable from the source.\"]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
