{"id": "59df6597-5a74-4873-8b41-e82f2ea4cabf", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:40:14.291635", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "7087586e-2c8d-43fc-a1b0-cd5b0fe9625a", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "The researcher approved and wants the final design document with five conditions. I should write a complete design in the answer field of end_researcher_turn with stage=result, with evidence containing feasibility checks and repo observations.\n\nLet me do a couple of quick verification commands to reconfirm feasibility constraints (I already have them, but maybe re-verify a couple of things for the feasibility section — e.g., pip download offline availability, whether pip can install from local wheels cache, disk space). Actually a small extra check: is there a pip cache / local wheel dir? And check disk space for potential offline install. That is a legitimate feasibility check for the \"what must be added\" section.\n\nLet me run: pip cache dir/size, df -h /workspace, check for any local wheelhouse, check if pip can reach index (already known no), check whether python3 -m venv works.\n\nThen write the final document.\n\nDesign document structure:\n\n1. Question & verdict target\n2. Unit of analysis & pairing\n3. Arms with tiering (a)\n4. Metrics: primary/secondary\n5. Pre-registered difficulty strata\n6. Statistical analysis plan: McNemar exact, mixed logistic with task random intercept, token-matched subset, dose-response\n7. Verdict rule (b)\n8. Placeholders with \"UNSPECIFIED\" tags + feasibility impact (c)\n9. Prerequisites to execute (d) — what must be added\n10. Residual limitations & failure modes (e)\n11. Fact vs assumption lists\n12. Reporting plan (parse-failure as scaffold artifact)\n\nLet me be careful with the verdict rule: define Δ = p(CoT) - p(no-CoT format-matched) on paired task-level success, averaged over strata (or stratified CMH estimate). Minimal meaningful difference δ_min — pragmatic choice, propose δ_min = 0.05 absolute (UNSPECIFIED/pragmatic,