{"id": "64237932-71e2-45be-9e4e-392a515dccb8", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:44:43.759637", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "0e518950-302f-4d6d-9a68-44c83ca9b01d", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Good — additional verified facts: no wheelhouse, no pip cache (0 bytes) so offline install of numpy/scipy impossible, no chromium/chrome (firefox present but no automation driver verified), venv creation fails to bootstrap pip (ensurepip error), 68G free on the workspace mount, /tmp tmpfs 1TB.\n\nNow write the final design document with all five conditions (a)-(e).\n\nLet me structure it:\n\n# अंतिम प्रयोग-डिज़ाइन (design-only; no execution)\n\n0. Scope & what this document is\n1. Hypothesis & estimand\n2. Unit of analysis, pairing, environment reset requirement (fragility)\n3. Arms with tiering + one-sentence causal contrast each\n4. Prompt/protocol invariants (what is held fixed)\n5. Difficulty strata (pre-registered) + interaction\n6. Metrics: primary/secondary/tertiary\n7. Analysis plan: McNemar exact, mixed logistic with task random intercept, adjustment for length, per-protocol vs ITT for parse failure\n8. Verdict rule (pre-registered): minimal meaningful difference Δ_min, one-sided test, sign consistency across strata, gating condition (CoT vs filler must show reasoning-specific effect), pragmatic choice flag\n9. Sample size / power sketch with formula and placeholders\n10. Randomization/counterbalancing/procedural controls\n11. Placeholders table: unspecified → what it makes fragile\n12. Feasibility: verified environment limits; execution prerequisites (the \"must-acquire\" list)\n13. Residual limitations / \"design fails in this way\"\n14. Facts (S) vs assumptions (A) two lists\n15. Open clarification questions (carried, unanswered)\n\nMust include for each arm the causal contrast in one sentence. Arms:\n\nTier-1 (minimum identification set):\n- A0 `no-CoT, format-matched`: emits the same JSON schema with an empty/\"—\" reasoning field. Contrast: baseline policy