.05 absolute (5 pp) — but must mark as pragmatic/researcher choice, not source-derived. Better: state rule symbolically (Δ_min = δ) and offer candidate calibration methods: (i) fixed 5 pp, (ii) half of the no-CoT arm's own seed-to-seed SD, (iii) one published-baseline gap. Recommend (i) or (ii) with a concrete number only as illustrative. That respects condition (b) \"एक minimal meaningful difference ... स्पष्ट लिखिए\" — they want a concrete rule. I'll give: δ = 0.05 absolute as primary, with alternative calibration if suite size makes 5pp unresolvable, and flag it as pragmatic.\n- Decision rule: \n  - \"Improve\" declared iff (1) one-sided exact McNemar p < α (α=0.025 one-sided, family = primary pair only), (2) point estimate D̂ ≥ δ, (3) lower bound of two-sided 95% CI... use one-sided 97.5% lower bound > 0, (4) reasoning-specificity gate: A1−A2 (CoT vs filler) must be ≥ 0 and its CI must exclude a pre-specified harm/dead-zone; if A1−A2 ≈ 0 and A2−A0 ≈ D̂, the verdict is \"gain attributable to verbosity/extra tokens, not reasoning\" → answer = \"no reasoning-specific improvement\".\n  - (5) sign consistency: CoT ≥ no-CoT in ≥ 2/3 of pre-registered difficulty strata (or: no stratum showing statistically reliable reversal at α_strat with multiplicity note), i.e., pooled improvement not driven by one family.\n  - \"Inconclusive\" branch: if discordant pair count < required for power (pre-registered MDE not resolvable), report as underpowered rather than null.\n  - \"Harm\" branch: symmetric one-sided test.\n  - Secondary verdict for the identification question, decoupled from headline.\n\nAnalysis plan:\n- Primary: exact McNemar on paired (per task, collapsing seeds via majority/any-success? careful). Define pairing unit precisely: primary pairing at task level with per-task success defined as ≥1 success in k seeds (\"solved within k attempts\") or as mean of k binaries entered into GLMM. I'll define: primary McNemar at task level using per-task success indicator = success in the modal/first seed run (avoid k-collapsing ambiguity) — actually simplest: primary unit = (task × seed) pair, matched within same task and same seed → McNemar over pairs; GLMM as robustness with seed as replicate. Let me specify: Primary: McNemar over (task,seed)-matched pairs — but McNemar assumes independent pairs; multiple seeds from the same task break independence → use cluster-bootstrap / stratified McNemar by task (exact per task not possible). Cleaner: GLMM primary with task random intercept and condition fixed effect, paired within task, and McNemar-exact reported on the task-level collapsed data (one representative seed per task) as the pre-registered simple primary. Hmm. The researcher accepted \"McNemar exact + task-level random intercept mixed logistic\". I'll present: Primary analysis = exact conditional McNemar on task-collapsed binary outcomes (one episode per task per condition, seed r=1 pre-registered) — exact conditional test is valid for a single binary pair per task. Robustness/primary-confirmatory secondary = mixed logistic with (1|task), all seeds, and stratum interaction. That's technically sound: McNemar's exact test via binomial on discordant pairs; the conditional MLE interpretation = logistic with task fixed effects. Good.\n- Length adjustment: mixed logistic adding (i) log total prompt+completion tokens per episode as covariate (ii) per-step output length; (iii) matched-token-budget subset analysis (restrict to episodes where CoT and control trajectory lengths within ±10%); (iv) reported as sensitivity, not primary, because conditioning on post-treatment variable can induce bias — must state that.\n- Difficulty interaction: condition × stratum term, LRT, and stratum-specific D̂ with CIs; pre-registered multiplicity handling (Holm within strata).\n- Parse-failure: pre-registered dual reporting: ITT (malformed/unparseable action = failure, capability-neutral? No — treat as scaffold artifact) → report ITT (any failure counts as failure) AND format-recovered analysis (retry-once with schema reminder, identical policy in both arms) AND descriptive parse-failure rate per arm with paired test. Verdict based on ITT; claims about \"capability\" must not be made from parse-failure asymmetry alone.\n- Missing/timeout: pre-registered handling; timeout = failure in ITT, sensitivity excluding infra-error episodes; infra errors (API 5xx, env crash) symmetric-exclusion rule decided blind to condition (pre-registered: exclude only episodes failing before step 1, both arms re-run).\n\nSample size/power: McNemar power depends on discordance rates p01, p10 — unknown until pilot; formula for required number of pairs n = ((z_{1-α}+z_{1-β})·sqrt(p̄_d) ...). Simpler: give the standard formula: n = (z_{1-α/2}√p_d + z_{1-β}√(p_d - δ²))² / δ² where p_d = p01+p10. Provide pilot step: run 30-task pilot to estimate p_d and per-stratum baseline success, then solve for n. Since baseline success unknown (WorkArena++ published numbers recall-only, and reuse-unknown), state n as a derived quantity → placeholder.\n\nRandomization & counterbalancing:\n- task order randomized once; condition order per task randomized ABBA/BAAB across tasks so half tasks start with CoT (guards against environment warm-up/state drift and against any session-level contamination); if a task requires session state, run arms in fresh sessions.\n- Fixed: model snapshot ID, decoding (temp=0 top_p=1 primary; temp>0 replicate arm for variance), max steps, system prompt, observation serialization, truncation policy, memory/history policy, tool/action space, tool-result verbosity, environment snapshot/data seed, agent code commit hash, retries, timeouts, logging.\n- Blinding of analysis: analysis script written before unblinding of aggregate outcome; condition labels coded A0/A1/A2 in logs, decoded only at analysis stage (guards HARKing).\n- Prompt-length audit: measure per-arm token counts and publish them (the diagnostic that makes the length confound